; The residual the report named: TUR-E0713 rejects a definition in tail position,
; but only for definition kinds that keep a distinct Expr kind AND match an exact
; source head -- so a definition that arrives via MACRO EXPANSION, and has
; already collapsed to EX_NIL_LIT by the time the body is checked, slipped past
; it and returned 0 silently.
;
; The general nil-tail check catches it, which is the argument the report made
; for doing the general fix rather than extending TUR-E0713's head list.
; A definition written literally in tail position still gets TUR-E0713's more
; specific "check for a missing close paren" message -- that diagnostic is not
; subsumed, it fires first.
;
; See docs/archive/nil-tail-not-checked-against-declared-return.md.
;
; The template is a quasiquote: a quoted list is data (quote-list-data-plan),
; so `(quote (defclass ...))` would expand to a Datum, not a definition.
(defmacro make-a-class [] `(defclass Foo [a] (bar [x] : int)))

(defn f [] : int (make-a-class))

(defn main [] : int (f))
